{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Capabilities will be split into three maps in the channel config: root channel, application, and orderer.",
    "Binaries not supporting required capabilities will crash intentionally in v1.1 to ensure data integrity.",
    "Orderer capabilities must be enabled before application capabilities to prevent blockchain forks during upgrades.",
    "Read-Your-Writes (RYW) will be implemented via a new API method in the chaincode shim.",
    "MSPConfig will be refactored into an interface to allow channel config block construction outside of configtxgen.",
    "The new lifecycle validation interface will return an automatically generated signature policy for '+lifecycle' requiring majority of orgs to endorse."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer is highly familiar with the Hyperledger Fabric codebase and Go programming language.",
    "Existing CI/CD pipelines and test environments are available and functional.",
    "Video recording and editing tools are readily available for the organization addition documentation.",
    "Effort estimates include design, coding, unit testing, and code review, but exclude long-term maintenance.",
    "'World config' refers to the standard test network configuration format used in Fabric."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Capabilities Framework Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Capabilities Framework including the three config maps, crash logic for unsupported binaries, upgrade order enforcement, and the <component>Capabilities interfaces.",
      "most_likely_effort": 15
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Chaincode RYW API",
      "activity_description": "Implement the Read-Your-Writes feature in the chaincode shim to optionally access already updated keys during the active transaction.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Network Org Addition Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Create a PPT diagram and record a video detailing the process of adding an organization to a running Fabric network without downtime.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "CouchDB Query Performance Monitoring",
      "activity_description": "Implement or integrate performance metrics and reporting for Fabric queries when CouchDB is used as the state database.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Configtxgen Refactoring & MSPConfig Interface",
      "activity_description": "Refactor MSPConfig into an interface to allow the construction of channel config blocks outside of the configtxgen tool.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Chaincode Singleton Removal",
      "activity_description": "Refactor and remove assorted chaincode singletons to prepare for the new lifecycle work and improve testability.",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Test Config Generation from World Config",
      "activity_description": "Update the test harness to generate peer core.yaml and orderer.yaml configuration files based on the values set in the World config.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Lifecycle Validation Parameters Interface",
      "activity_description": "Implement the new lifecycle interface returning validation parameters for chaincode, including the '+lifecycle' edge case with an auto-generated majority-of-orgs signature policy.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 56
  }
}
```

